A||||6||fyerstarter||Can you access the fuel pump without removing the tank?||||1||
Z||000000||fyerstarter||04-21-2001||12:54 PM||||Hey I was just wondering if since the fule tank seems to occupy some of the center console area if it is possible to gain acess to the fuel pump by removing some interior peices rather than dropping the tank? Has anyone tried this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroparts.com||04-21-2001||12:57 PM||||No you can not!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Raydar||04-21-2001||12:57 PM||||Fyerstarter. <BR>No. Sorry. The pump is actually in the tank. The entire sender/pump/screen is removed from the tank as an assembly. The only way to access it is to drop the tank. Solid metal above it, with the tank in place.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||kinboyatuwo||04-21-2001||04:26 PM||||Never say no!<P>you could remove all interior stuff in the way and cut through with a torch<P>easier the other way, pluss a torch and gas tank do not mix well unless you are experienced!!<P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||4
